color":"7057ff","default":true,"description":"Good for newcomers"},{"id":9485588341,"node_id":"LA_kwDOPT4Fuc8AAAACNWKXdQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/INDIGOAZUL/la-tanda-web/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"FFD700","default":false,"description":"Rewards available in LTD tokens"},{"id":10394123360,"node_id":"LA_kwDOPT4Fuc8AAAACa4m8YA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/INDIGOAZUL/la-tanda-web/labels/tier-0","name":"tier-0","color":"7057ff","default":false,"description":"Beginner: docs, translation, tests (10-50 LTD)"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":126,"created_at":"2026-03-01T17:12:36Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T08:17:46Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# Developer Documentation Improvements — 50 LTD Bounty (Tier 0)\n\n**Tier:** 0 (anyone can claim)\n\n## Task\nImprove the README.md with better onboarding information for new developers.\n\n## Scope\n- **File to modify:** `README.md` only\n- **Do NOT** create new doc files (no `docs/GUIDE.md` or similar)\n- The project already has a [Dev Portal](https://latanda.online/dev-dashboard.html) — don't duplicate it\n\n## Requirements\n1. Add a \"Development Setup\" section explaining how to serve locally (`npx serve .`)\n2. Add a \"Project Structure\" section explaining the key directories (match what's in CONTRIBUTING.md)\n3. Ensure all links work (Swagger UI, Dev Portal, Chain Explorer)\n4. All text in English (README is developer-facing)\n\n## Definition of Done\n- [ ] README has clear development setup instructions\n- [ ] Project structure section matches reality\n- [ ] All links verified working\n- [ ] No duplicate content from CONTRIBUTING.md\n\n## Codebase Verification Question\n> To claim this bounty, answer: **Where does `marketplace-social.js` live — in `js/` or at the HTML root? What is the name of the main API file?**\n\n## Estimated Time\n1-2 hours.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/INDIGOAZUL/la-tanda-web/issues/50/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/INDIGOAZUL/la-tanda-web/issues/50/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jnoecker/AmbonMUD/issues/1396","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jnoecker/AmbonMUD","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jnoecker/AmbonMUD/issues/1396/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jnoecker/AmbonMUD/issues/1396/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jnoecker/AmbonMUD/issues/1396/events","html_url":"https://github.com/jnoecker/AmbonMUD/issues/1396","id":4814752717,"node_id":"I_kwDORAkiac8AAAABHvtLzQ","number":1396,"title":"Akathavae: daily illumination commissions (new illuminate daily-quest type)","user":{"login":"jnoecker","id":1014858,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTQ4NTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1014858?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnoecker","html_url":"https://github.com/jnoecker","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnoecker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnoecker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnoecker/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnoecker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnoecker/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnoecker/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnoecker/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnoecker/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jnoecker/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10058206877,"node_id":"LA_kwDORAkiac8AAAACV4QOnQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jnoecker/AmbonMUD/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","color":"a2eeef","default":true,"description":"New feature or request"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-07-05T22:58:04Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T07:25:17Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Context\n\nThe daily-quest system (`DailyQuestSystem.kt`, config `DailyQuestsConfig` in `AppConfig.kt` ~line 1292) supports pool-defined dailies with objective types `kill, gather, dungeon, craft, pvpKill` (`DailyQuestDefinition.type`, `AppConfig.kt:1311–1313`). It is currently `enabled: false` with empty pools in the bundled `application.yaml` (~line 2737); the production instance enables systems via its R2 config overlay (out of scope for this repo — engine + example config only). The Akathavae success path is `AkathavaeSystem.resolveSuccess` (~line 163); it already fires `combat.creditIlluminationKill` → `callbacks.onMobKilledByPlayer` once per living mob instance. Line numbers as of main @ `7fe0c445`.\n\n## Problem\n\nOnce an Akathavae has recorded everything nearby, the only repeatable progression is 20% repeat-XP per subject on a 5-minute cooldown — a grind with no framing. Fighters will eventually get daily kill bounties; explorers need an equivalent: **illumination commissions** (\"the Arcanum requests: record 5 creatures today\").\n\n## Fix\n\n1. **First, verify double-counting**: because `creditIlluminationKill` routes through `onMobKilledByPlayer`, check whether illuminations *already* advance `kill`-type dailies (follow where daily-quest progress hooks into the kill callback chain). Document the finding in the PR. If they do, that's acceptable (parity!), but the new type below must count **only** illuminations so commissions stay path-flavored.\n2. Add an `illuminate` objective type to the daily system:\n   - Accept `\"illuminate\"` in `DailyQuestDefinition.type` (update the doc comment at `AppConfig.kt:1312` and any `validated()` type whitelist if one exists).\n   - Add a progress hook: `DailyQuestSystem.onIlluminated(sessionId)` (mirror the existing `onKill`/`onGather`-style entry points — find them and copy the shape).\n   - Call it from `AkathavaeSystem.resolveSuccess`, inside the once-per-living-instance credit block (~line 217), so a commission can't be farmed by re-illuminating one rat. `AkathavaeSystem` is constructed in `GameEngine.kt` ~line 817 — inject the daily system or a callback, matching how other systems receive cross-system hooks there.\n   - Decide and document: do **observations** (non-combatant NPCs, `observeNpc` ~line 260) count? Recommendation: yes, first-time observations count — commissions are about recording, not danger. First-time only (`firstTime` branch).\n3. Add 2–3 example `illuminate` entries to the bundled `dailyPool` in `application.yaml` **commented out or accompanying the existing empty-pool default** — whichever pattern keeps `validated()` happy with `enabled: false` (the validator requires `dailyPool.size >= dailySlots` only when relevant — check `AppConfig.kt:166`). Example: `{type: illuminate, targetCount: 5, description: \"The Arcanum requests five fresh accounts of living creatures.\", goldReward: 150, xpReward: 400}`. The gold reward matters: Akathavae have no kill-gold income.\n4. GMCP: daily quests already emit via the `Quest` package family (`QuestDailyPayload`, `GmcpEmitter.kt` ~line 3629) — new type should flow through with no transport change; verify the web client's daily-quest UI renders an unknown type string gracefully (it should just display description/progress).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- With dailies enabled in test config and an `illuminate` commission active: successful first-time illuminations and observations advance it; repeat illuminations of the same living instance do not; kills do not.\n- Completion pays the configured gold/XP and respects the existing streak bonus.\n- Existing daily types unaffected; `enabled: false` default boots clean.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `DailyQuestSystem` tests exist — extend with the new type (enabled config, `MutableClock` for reset boundaries).\n- Integration-style test: pledge → accept commission → illuminate N distinct mobs → completed.\n- `./gradlew ktlintCheck test integrationTest`.\n\n## Workflow\n\nFeature branch from `main`, one focused PR.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jnoecker/AmbonMUD/issues/1396/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jnoecker/AmbonMUD/issues/1396/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/issues/76","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/issues/76/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/issues/76/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/issues/76/events","html_url":"https://github.com/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/issues/76","id":4776229449,"node_id":"I_kwDOTGNm188AAAABHK96SQ","number":76,"title":"[BUG] Unvalidated Redirect in Login Page $10","user":{"login":"zhangjiayang6835-cyber","id":288065324,"node_id":"U_kgDOESuHLA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/288065324?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhangjiayang6835-cyber","html_url":"https://github.com/zhangjiaya