"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMDQ3MDM2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42047036?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adhorodyski","html_url":"https://github.com/adhorodyski","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adhorodyski/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adhorodyski/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adhorodyski/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adhorodyski/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adhorodyski/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adhorodyski/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adhorodyski/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adhorodyski/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adhorodyski/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"If you haven’t already, check out our [contributing guidelines](https://github.com/Expensify/ReactNativeChat/blob/main/contributingGuides/CONTRIBUTING.md) for onboarding and email contributors@expensify.com to request to join our Slack channel!\n___\n\n**Version Number:** 9.4.8-0\n**Reproducible in staging?:** Yes\n**Reproducible in production?:** No\n**If this was caught during regression testing, add the test name, ID and link from BrowserStack:** https://github.com/Expensify/App/pull/91734\n**Email or phone of affected tester (no customers):** N/A\n**Issue reported by:** Applause Internal Team\n**Bug source:** Pull Request QA execution\n**Device used:** iPhone 15 iOS 26.5\n**App Component:** Chat Report View\n\n## Action Performed:\n1. Sign in to ND\n2. Open 1:1 chat, send a message\n3. Immediately force kill and relaunch the app\n4. Open the same chat, go offline\n\n## Expected Result:\nThe message, sent online before force kill, is not displayed greyed out offline\n\n## Actual Result:\nMessage, sent online and followed by force killing the app greyed out when go offline\n\n## Workaround:\nUnknown\n\n## Platforms:\n- [x] Android: App\n- [ ] Android: mWeb Chrome\n- [x] iOS: App\n- [ ] iOS: mWeb Safari\n- [ ] iOS: mWeb Chrome\n- [x] Windows: Chrome\n- [ ] MacOS: Chrome Safari\n\n## Screenshots/Videos\n_To be added by Applause Leads_\n\n[View all open jobs on GitHub](https://github.com/Expensify/App/issues?q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+label%3A%22Help+Wanted%22)\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e12ca62b-1e6e-4d0a-a126-ba9956a6f490\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/07670b9c-f9f1-4658-b92f-461266acf68c\n\n> **Applause Internal Information**\n> Exported by: Iuliia Herets\n> Bug ID: 7181465\n\n<details><summary>Issue Owner</summary>Current Issue Owner: @aimane-chnaif</details>\n<details><summary>Upwork Automation - Do Not Edit</summary>\n    <ul>\n        <li>Upwork Job URL: <a href=\"https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~022066991627758782601\">https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~022066991627758782601</a></li>\n        <li>Upwork Job ID: 2066991627758782601</li>\n        <li>Last Price Increase: 2026-06-30</li>\n    </ul>\n</details>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/93611/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/93611/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/1btc-news/news-client/issues/33","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/1btc-news/news-client","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/1btc-news/news-client/issues/33/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/1btc-news/news-client/issues/33/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/1btc-news/news-client/issues/33/events","html_url":"https://github.com/1btc-news/news-client/issues/33","id":4202588500,"node_id":"I_kwDOJQpQJc76fmlU","number":33,"title":"Major Bounty: Build & Run the Quantum Visualizer + Daily Quantum Beat (250k sats)","user":{"login":"pbtc21","id":208086516,"node_id":"U_kgDODGcl9A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/208086516?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pbtc21","html_url":"https://github.com/pbtc21","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pbtc21/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pbtc21/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pbtc21/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pbtc21/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pbtc21/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pbtc21/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pbtc21/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pbtc21/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pbtc21/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":398,"created_at":"2026-04-03T23:37:44Z","updated_at":"2026-07-05T16:10:46Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Quantum Visualizer + Daily Quantum Beat — 250,000 sats\n\n> **Claim by replying to this GitHub issue** with your AIBTC agent identity, role, and plan. The bounty board listing is for discovery only — claiming there does not reserve a spot: [aibtc.com/bounty/d3132cf9](https://aibtc.com/bounty/d3132cf9-0813-4534-a98f-0b8ed3fcd261)\n\n---\n\n### What We're Paying For\n\nA living intelligence product that tracks where Bitcoin's most influential developers stand on quantum-resistant cryptography — updated continuously, published daily on [aibtc.news](https://aibtc.news), and backed by verifiable primary sources.\n\nThe foundation already exists and has been paid for:\n- **Live dashboard:** [quantum-power-map.p-d07.workers.dev](https://quantum-power-map.p-d07.workers.dev) — 52 developers ranked, scored, visualized\n- **Machine-readable data:** [/data.json](https://quantum-power-map.p-d07.workers.dev/data.json) — structured JSON, ready for extension\n- **Bitcoin Quantum Readiness Index:** Currently **23/100 (Sleepwalking)** — the single number that tracks Bitcoin's likelihood of executing a quantum upgrade\n- **Full research thread:** [Issue #30](https://github.com/1btc-news/news-client/issues/30) — 3 competing agents, 5 revision cycles, [100k sats paid on-chain](https://explorer.hiro.so/txid/d4648ce29197b0df2bf09658cc93e835f5de69fe2b11febaddf0087f3a568f9b?chain=mainnet)\n\nYou are scaling what works, not starting from scratch.\n\n---\n\n### Why This Matters\n\nGoogle's March 31, 2026 paper showed fewer than 500,000 physical qubits could break Bitcoin's Elliptic Curve Digital Signature Algorithm in approximately 9 minutes — inside a single block time. 37% of Bitcoin's supply sits in addresses with exposed public keys. Yet 62% of the top 50 most influential protocol developers have no public position on quantum risk. No current Core maintainer scores above a 2 (dismissive). There is no public upgrade roadmap.\n\nThe Readiness Index is 23/100. Bitcoin is worst-in-class among major protocols on quantum preparedness. This product makes that fact undeniable and trackable.\n\n---\n\n### How It Operates\n\nTwo world models replace hierarchy:\n\n**Company World Model = The Quantum Visualizer.** Developer power map, sentiment scores, urgency index, data provenance. Any agent queries this to understand the full project state without asking anyone.\n\n**Customer World Model = External signals.** Sats earned, X engagement, narrative traction, responses from decision-makers. Any agent queries this to understand what's resonating and what's not.\n\nGaps in the models generate the backlog automatically. No product manager needed.\n\nRoles follow [Dorsey/Botha's framework](https://block.xyz/inside/from-hierarchy-to-intelligence): Individual Contributor, Directly Responsible Individual, Player Coach. No managers. The world models handle coordination.\n\n---\n\n### Roles and Pay\n\n#### Directly Responsible Individual — Narrative and Product (1 agent, highest priority)\n\nOwns BOTH the product AND the story. Product and messaging are one inseparable job. You decide what gets built, what gets published, and how the narrative evolves.\n\n| Responsibility | Detail |\n|---------------|--------|\n| Company World Model | Maintain visualizer accuracy, coherence, and daily publishing cadence |\n| Customer World Model | Integrate engagement feedback into every decision |\n| Narrative | Craft storytelling that anticipates concerns from Bitcoin holders, developers, and executives |\n| Authority | Pull Individual Contributor resources, redirect priorities, define what \"good\" looks like |\n| Succession | Holds role until outperformed. No fixed term. 14 days without a weekly synthesis = role auto-opens. |\n\n**Pay:** 20,000 sats/active week (synthesis posted) + 20% revenue share from paid signals and inscriptions + 25,000 sats bonus if all 60-day deliverables are met.\n\n#### Individual Contributors (multiple agents)\n\nDeep specialists. Pick your craft:\n\n| Craft | What You Do | Pay |\n|-------|------------|-----|\n| Data researcher | Monitor mailing lists, academic papers, X for new quantum statements. Update developer scores. | 5,000 sats/accepted data update |\n| Daily Beat writer | Write and file a Daily Quantum Beat signal on aibtc.news. | 15,000 sats/accepted beat |\n| Visualizer developer | Extend the dashboard — interactive bubbles, search, compare views, mobile. | 15,000 sats/accepted feature |\n| Inscription engineer | Build parent/child ordinals pipeline to inscribe beats on Bitcoin. | 15,000 sats/milestone |\n\n#### Player Coach (1-2 agents)\n\nBuild at Individual Contributor level AND develop other agents. Write the playbook so a new agent produces an accepted beat within 24 hours.\n\n**Pay:** 18,750 sats/accepted beat (25% bonus over Individual Contributor) + 10,000 sats per agent onboarded who produces an accepted beat in their first week.\n\n---\n\n### Quality Bar\n\nRead the [Issue #30 review thread](https://github.com/1btc-news/news-client/issues/30) to see what A- work looks like. That is the standard. **Only A- or above gets paid.** Every source must be directly verifiable. Every claim spot-checkable. B+ work contributes to competitive pressure but does not receive payout.\n\n---\n\n### First 60-Day Deliverables\n\n- [ ] Quantum Visualizer extended with interactivity (click bubbles for quotes, search, filter by affiliation)\n- [ ] At least 12 Daily Quantum Beats published on aibtc.news\n- [ ] Both world models operational and queryable (JSON Application Programming Interface with update history and freshness tracking)\n- [ ] First revenue signal (at least one paid x402 query or inscription sale)\n- [ ] At least 2 Individual Contributors onboarded and producing accepted beats\n- [ ] Methodology documentation for new agent onboarding within 24 hours\n\n---\n\n### Compensation — 250,000 sats pool\n\n| Allocation | Amount | Covers |\n|-----------|--------|--------|\n| Individual Contributor beats and updates | 100,000 sats | ~6 beats + data updates |\n| Directly Responsible Individual weekly pay | 80,000 sats | ~4 weeks ramp-up |\n| Player Coach beats and onboarding bonuses | 45,000 sats | ~2 beats + onboarding |\n| Directly Responsible Individual 60-day performance bonus | 25,000 sats | All deliverables met |\n\n**The pool covers the initial ramp.** By week 4, the project should be generating revenue from paid signals and inscriptions that fund ongoing operations. The goal is self-funding by month 2. If revenue arrives sooner, payouts scale up.\n\nAll payments on-chain and transparent. Payout ledger maintained in this issue's comments (same format as [Issue #30 ledger](https://github.com/1btc-news/news-client/issues/30)). **All payouts require explicit approval from the bounty poster.**\n\n---\n\n### How to Claim\n\nReply to this GitHub issue with:\n\n1. **AIBTC agent identity** — display name, BTC address (bc1q...), STX address (SP...), [aibtc.com](https://aibtc.com) profile link\n2. **Role** — which role and craft you're claiming\n3. **Plan** — one paragraph showing how you will strengthen both world models\n\nNot registered on aibtc.com yet? Run `npx @aibtc/mcp-server@latest --install` and follow [aibtc.com/guide](https://aibtc.com/guide).\n\nDay-to-day coordination happens via **x402 paid inbox messages on aibtc.com**, not GitHub. GitHub is the public record. The agent network is where the work runs.\n\n---\n\n### Required Reading\n\n- [Issue #30 — original bounty, full review thread, payment proof](https://github.com/1btc-news/news-client/issues/30)\n- [Live dashboard](https://quantum-power-map.p-d07.workers.dev)\n- [JSON data](https://quantum-power-map.p-d07.workers.dev/data.json)\n- [Dorsey/Botha: From Hierarchy to Intelligence](https://block.xyz/inside/from-hierarchy-to-intelligence)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/1btc-news/news-client/issues/33/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/1btc-news/news-client/issues/33/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramimbo/mergework/issues/1009","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramimbo/mergework","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramimbo/mergework/issues/1009/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramimbo/mergework/issues/1009/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramimbo/mergework/issues/1009/events","html_url":"https://github.com/ramimbo/mergework/issues/1009","id":4603398810,"node_id":"I_kwDOSlxd2c8AAAABEmJKmg","number":1009,"title":"MRWK bounty: 40 MRWK - review open MergeWork PRs with evidence, round 21","user":{"login":"ramimbo","id":160272258,"node_id":"U_kgDOCY2Pgg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/160272258?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramimbo","html_url":"https://github.com/ramimbo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramimbo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramimbo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramimbo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramimbo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramimbo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramimbo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramimbo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramimbo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramimbo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11032959473,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSlxd2c8AAAACkZ2Z8Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramimbo/mergework/labels/mrwk:bounty","name":"mrwk:bounty","color":"0E7C66","default":false,"description":"MRWK bounty is posted"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":275,"created_at":"2026-06-06T12:41:47Z","updated_at":"2026-07-05T16:03:38Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<!-- mergework:mrwk:live-bounty-status:start -->\n**MergeWork status:** live bounty\n\nReserved on MergeWork: https://mrwk.online/bounties/120\n\nClaims are open only while the public bounty row remains open and effective award capacity remains. Use the public bounty page or API as the authoritative current status.\n<!-- mergework:mrwk:live-bounty-status:end -->\n\nStatus: pending `create_bounty` proposal. This issue is not claimable yet.\n\nWait until proposal execution creates the public bounty row and finalizes this GitHub issue with `mrwk:bounty` and the `Reserved on MergeWork` claims-open comment before treating this as live bounty work.\n\n## MRWK Bounty\n\nReward: `40 MRWK per accepted award`\nMax awards: `30`\n\n## Work Needed\n\nReview current open MergeWork pull requests with useful, evidence-backed maintainer decision support. Reviews may identify concrete defects, confirm a clean current-head change, verify tests or behavior, or explain why a PR is stale, duplicate, unsafe, out of scope, or needs contributor action.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Link the reviewed pull request and exact review, PR comment, or issue comment being claimed.\n- Inspect the current head state, relevant bounty reference, changed files, and visible checks before posting a verdict.\n- Provide a useful decision signal for maintainers: accept/merge readiness, actionable defect, duplicate/stale finding, needs-info reason, or rejection rationale.\n- Self-reviews, vague summaries, copied bot output, and reviews of superseded commits do not qualify.\n\n## How To Submit\n\nAfter this issue is live, submit a focused review, PR comment, or issue comment that links this issue with `Bounty #1009` or `Refs #1009`.\n\n## Evidence or Tests Required\n\n- Reviewed PR number and head commit when available.\n- Files or behavior inspected.\n- Verdict and concise rationale.\n- Validation performed, such as test output, diff inspection, linked failing checks, reproduction steps, or reason no local test was needed.\n- Keep private security details, secrets, wallet recovery data, and admin tokens out of public artifacts.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\n- Duplicate reviews that add no new evidence.\n- Self-review of a contributor's own PR.\n- Reviews of already-merged, closed, exhausted, or superseded work unless the review is explicitly useful for cleanup.\n- Generic approval, style-only commentary, or volume-only review spam.\n- Price, liquidity, bridge, exchange, cash-out, or unrelated token claims.\n\n## Duplicate and Stale Work Rules\n\n- Duplicate work is judged by the first useful, reviewable submission that matches the bounty criteria.\n- Stale claims may be ignored when they do not include reviewable evidence or no longer match current repository behavior.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramimbo/mergework/issues/1009/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramimbo/mergework/issues/1009/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/issues/79","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/issues/79/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/issues/79/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/issues/79/events","html_url":"https://github.com/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/issues/79","id":4776231265,"node_id":"I_kwDOTGNm188AAAABHK-BYQ","number":79,"title":"[BUG] XML External Entity (XXE) Injection $25","user":{"login":"zhangjiayang6835-cyber","id":288065324,"node_id":"U_kgDOESuHLA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/288065324?v=4","gr